DTEND:20261007T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:GW Chicago Reception with Elliott School Dean Alyssa AyresDate 
 and TimeTuesday‚ October 6\n6:00 pm - 8:00 pm\n\nLocationUniversity Club
  of Chicago\n76 East Monroe Street\nChicago‚ IL 60603\n\nEvent Descripti
 onThe GW community in Chicago is invited to join us for a reception and di
 scussion with Elliott School Dean Alyssa Ayres. Our alumni panelists will 
 discuss their varied careers in international affairs. Panelists to be ann
 ounced. \n\nRegistration for the event is $15 for alumni‚ parents‚ and
  guests‚ and includes hors d’oeuvres‚ beer‚ wine‚ and soft drink
 s. Students are free.\n\nSpeakersMarty Mannion‚ ESIA BA ’97‚ is Co-H
 ead of TD Securities Automated Trading LLC (TDSAT)‚ the quantitative fix
 ed income division of TD Securities. TDSAT is a market leader in municipal
  and corporate bonds.  Mr. Mannion was previously co-CEO of Headlands Tech
  Global Markets‚ LLC (HTGM)‚ where he helped build the firm’s fixed 
 income trading business. TD Bank acquired HTGM in July 2021. Prior to join
 ing Headlands‚ Mr. Mannion was Chief Operating Officer and Managing Dire
 ctor of Citadel Execution Services‚ the U.S. equity and options market m
 aking division of Citadel Securities. Mr. Mannion joined Citadel in 2004
 ‚ and during his 8+ year tenure helped to build the division into one of
  the leading liquidity and execution providers in U.S. listed equities and
  equity options. Prior to joining Citadel in 2004‚ Mr. Mannion spent 4 y
 ears at the NASDAQ and 2 years at Economists‚ Inc. Mr. Mannion has serve
 d on several boards‚ including: DirectEdge Holdings‚ an electronic tra
 ding system for U.S.-listed equities\; EASDAQ‚ which owned and operated 
 Equiduct Systems Ltd.‚ an electronic exchange for European equities\; an
 d NYSE Amex‚ the NYSE-operated U.S. listed equity options exchange.\n\n 
 \n\n\n\nAppointed in February 2021‚ Alyssa Ayres is the first woman to s
 erve as permanent dean at the Elliott School. She is a foreign policy prac
 titioner and award-winning author with senior experience in the government
 ‚ nonprofit‚ and private sectors. From 2013 to 2021‚ she was a senio
 r fellow for India‚ Pakistan‚ and South Asia at the Council on Foreign
  Relations‚ where she remains an adjunct senior fellow‚ and from 2010 
 to 2013 served as deputy assistant secretary of state for South Asia. Her 
 work focuses primarily on India’s role in the world and on U.S. relation
 s with South Asia in the larger Indo-Pacific. Ayres received an AB from Ha
 rvard College and an MA and PhD from the University of Chicago. She is a m
 ember of the Council on Foreign Relations‚ the Trilateral Commission‚ 
 the Halifax International Security Forum’s agenda group‚ and serves on
  the board of directors of the National Endowment for Democracy and the Wo
 men’s Foreign Policy Group. In 2021 and 2022‚ the Washingtonian includ
 ed her as one of their “most influential people shaping policy.”
GEO:41.88325;-87.632388
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:GW Chicago Reception with Elliott School Dean Alyssa Ayres (Chicago
 &sbquo\; IL)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/gw-chicago-reception-with-elli
 ott-school-dean-alyssa-ayres-chicagosbquo-il
CATEGORIES:Alumni
END:VEVENT
