DESCRIPTION:Economic competition between the United States and China has be
 en a defining issue of the twenty-first century. But after years of rapid 
 growth\, China’s economy has faltered. How did its long-term economic ou
 tlook change so quickly? And can Beijing change course and preserve China
 ’s political ambition for global economic primacy?\n\nIn Broken China\, 
 Logan Wright offers an unflinching account of how China’s economy hit th
 e wall. Drawing on extensive experience analyzing the Chinese financial se
 ctor on the ground\, he argues that China’s economic slowdown is rooted 
 in its financial system\, and an unprecedented credit expansion is finally
  coming to an end. Rather than crisis or collapse\, Wright argues\, China 
 is suffering from a decay of its economic policy tools. With no clear path
  to recovery\, China’s economy is broken\, the consequences of which wil
 l reverberate around the world.\n\nDoors will open no sooner than 15 minut
 es before the event start time.\n\nThe Elliott School can coordinate with 
 the university to reasonably accommodate most disabilities. If you need sp
 ecific accommodations\, please contact the Sigur Center at gsigur@gwu.edu.
  Requests should be made as soon as possible\, but at least three days pri
 or to the program to ensure accommodation.
GEO:38.896188;-77.044206
LOCATION:1957 E Street NW\, Room 505
SUMMARY:China's Challenge: "Broken China: How the Economic Miracle Shattere
 d and What it Means for the World"
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/chinas-challenge-broken-china-
 how-the-economic-miracle-shattered-and-what-it-means-for-the-world
CATEGORIES:Academic
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Speakers
CATEGORIES:International
