DESCRIPTION:IDDP's Food for Thought event series is designed to spark curio
 sity and conversation by bringing together faculty and university affiliat
 es who want to share their research with the broader university community.
  Each session highlights innovative work and invites open and insightful d
 iscussion across disciplines. Enjoy great ideas\, thoughtful dialogue—an
 d lunch is on us.\n\nKicking off our fall semester slate is Marc Lynch\, G
 W professor of political science and international affairs and director of
  the Project on Middle East Political Science (POMEPS). Professor Lynch wi
 ll analyze how digital technologies are deployed across the Middle East an
 d how they influence both regime resilience and public resistance. He will
  also explores the limits of digital surveillance\, highlighting cases whe
 re even advanced systems have failed to prevent unrest or anticipate major
  events.
GEO:38.899826;-77.046159
LOCATION:Media and Public Affairs Building\, IDDP Office\; Suite 201
SUMMARY:Digital Authoritarianism and Surveillance in the Middle East
